WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:01.450
Good morning.

00:00:01.450 --> 00:00:03.520
Good morning. Hey, today...

00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:04.020
Yeah?

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:06.810
We need an afro, 
joke glasses... and what else?

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:10.380
Did you stay up late last night?

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.690
Yeah, I couldn't figure 
out how to allocate...

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:15.490
our class's cultural festival budget.

00:00:15.940 --> 00:00:18.070
I was up all night thinking it over.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:24.760
You must be busy as both a class rep and
 a member of the student council.

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.660
It's even worse with the festival–

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.250
Shun-chan, Kanamecchi!

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.240
Morning!

00:00:32.290 --> 00:00:34.290
Shun, what's your class doing?

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:37.490
Oh, my class is...

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:39.080
Don't ignore me!

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:41.330
Where's my morning greeting?

00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:44.440
Theirs was the correct response.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:45.750
Yup.

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.190
I don't believe you two!

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.650
Um, Chizuru-kun...

00:00:49.650 --> 00:00:52.440
Ignore him. There's no point even replying.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:54.400
Shun, what's your class doing?

00:00:55.960 --> 00:00:58.740
We're doing a café with a twist.

00:00:59.030 --> 00:01:03.030
Yeah, everyone's gonna cross dress.

00:01:03.030 --> 00:01:04.250
Cross dress?

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:06.870
Really? Awesome!

00:01:06.870 --> 00:01:09.750
Kaname-kun, what is your class doing?

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.310
A stereotypical haunted house.

00:02:42.610 --> 00:02:44.850
There's not much time till the festival.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:49.810
Use this extended homeroom period
 effectively to work on your projects.

00:02:50.110 --> 00:02:51.280
That is all.

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.820
With the cultural festival 
approaching, the classroom...

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.090
is overflowing with 
unconcealable anticipation...

00:02:58.090 --> 00:02:59.820
comforting bustle...

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:01.530
and trouble.

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.920
Hey, Tsukahara-kun.

00:03:05.620 --> 00:03:09.170
What do you think of advertising by walking...

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:11.660
around school in costume with placards?

00:03:11.660 --> 00:03:12.710
Doesn't that sound interesting?

00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:14.080
What?

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:15.680
We've barely enough money as it is.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:17.210
We don't need to do that.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:18.210
We'll make posters.

00:03:18.510 --> 00:03:22.810
But you gotta go big or go home.

00:03:22.810 --> 00:03:24.050
That's right.

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.790
Well, Tsukahara-kun?

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:31.170
I'll see if we can shift some 
money from somewhere else.

00:03:31.170 --> 00:03:32.750
Great!

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.230
Thanks!

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:36.770
What should we do?

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:39.400
What about a kappa? That sounds good, doesn't it?

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:40.490
<b>Budget recalculation</b>

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:41.610
Hey, Tsukahara.

00:03:41.980 --> 00:03:45.370
How do I go about getting 
blackout curtains from the school?

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:48.790
What? You haven't gotten any yet?

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:51.090
If you don't hurry, someone else will get to them before us!

00:03:51.090 --> 00:03:52.750
Sorry, sorry.

00:03:52.750 --> 00:03:53.790
So, how do I get them?

00:03:54.970 --> 00:03:57.180
Go to the Student Council Office,

00:03:57.180 --> 00:04:01.780
get an equipment request form and fill out...

00:04:01.780 --> 00:04:03.230
That's too much work.

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.450
It's more work for me to 
explain it to you repeatedly!

00:04:05.450 --> 00:04:07.580
Tsukahara-kun, do you have a minute?

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.810
It's about the day of the festival.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:11.520
Could you look at this?

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:13.010
Oh, this is...

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:15.940
Hold on, Tsukahara. What about the curtains?

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.150
Tsu-ka-ha-ra.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.280
I'll do it!

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.740
You will?

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:25.160
Thanks, Tsukahara-kun.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:26.780
Shut up.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:31.090
<i>Why does everyone need my help?</i>

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:35.790
I guess we'll decide who'll 
be doing what later.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.280
Yeah, thanks.

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:48.040
Hey, Yuki and that monkey... I mean,
 Tachibana... where'd they go?

00:04:52.580 --> 00:04:53.970
Yu-ta.

00:04:53.970 --> 00:04:55.170
Shun-chan.

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:03.320
What are you doing? Don't 
you have homeroom, too?

00:05:03.670 --> 00:05:06.660
There's something I want to show you two.

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:09.820
Ta-da!

00:05:09.820 --> 00:05:11.780
Yuki and I made them!

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:14.510
Our environmentally-friendly eco-trains!

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:17.170
Half of the train is made out of kindness.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:20.670
Are you using that in your haunted house?

00:05:20.670 --> 00:05:22.420
What? No.

00:05:23.040 --> 00:05:25.290
They made it even though they won't use it...

00:05:25.790 --> 00:05:28.340
Even though they're busy with preparations...

00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:31.850
Yuta, get in. I'll pull you.

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:37.520
But we're in the middle of preparations.

00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:44.930
Maybe I'll go for a ride...

00:05:44.930 --> 00:05:46.250
Right, Yuki-kun?

00:05:48.530 --> 00:05:50.280
How is it, sir?

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:53.430
You look like a jack-in-a-box!

00:05:53.430 --> 00:05:55.190
Really?

00:05:55.190 --> 00:05:57.790
I feel like I've been crammed into a box...

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.210
Where would you like to go, sir?

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:01.890
We can go anywhere.

00:06:01.890 --> 00:06:05.010
Staying off the existing rails is our motto.

00:06:05.260 --> 00:06:07.270
Whose lazy son are you?

00:06:07.970 --> 00:06:11.190
Please take us to Azuma-sensei.

00:06:11.190 --> 00:06:13.510
There's something I want to borrow from him.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.240
Roger.

00:06:13.790 --> 00:06:15.240
Roger.

00:06:15.240 --> 00:06:17.650
The eco-train is departing.

00:06:32.780 --> 00:06:34.640
That's not fair!

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:37.880
Damn it!

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.700
I can't believe you installed a bottomless feature!

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:41.890
Why didn't I think of that?

00:06:41.890 --> 00:06:44.590
Since when did cardboard become so high-tech?

00:06:44.590 --> 00:06:47.790
You can trust me with your life, sir!

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:48.340
What?

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:50.260
Speed up!

00:06:51.950 --> 00:06:53.090
U-Um...

00:06:54.660 --> 00:06:56.150
Curve!

00:07:06.750 --> 00:07:09.030
And we've arrived.

00:07:09.350 --> 00:07:13.280
Uh, um... Chizuru-kun...

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:19.080
What's with th—

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:21.790
The sweat? Don't worry about it.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.030
Not the sweat.

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:24.960
What's that?

00:07:25.530 --> 00:07:27.730
Don't worry about it.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:30.230
I need you to...

00:07:31.110 --> 00:07:32.860
What was it?

00:07:34.270 --> 00:07:36.140
Azuma-sensei.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:40.210
I want to borrow some materials...

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:43.690
Another one? Is this a fad?

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:46.120
I'm not that sure.

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:48.330
You cheater, Yukki!

00:07:48.330 --> 00:07:49.780
I won't lose next time!

00:07:49.780 --> 00:07:52.190
I've installed my own bottomless feature!

00:07:52.190 --> 00:07:53.950
That's just broken, isn't it?

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:02.870
Will this do?

00:08:02.870 --> 00:08:05.140
Yes, thank you.

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:07.680
How are your preparations for 
the festival coming along?

00:08:08.080 --> 00:08:09.120
I trust it's going well?

00:08:09.120 --> 00:08:09.910
Yes.

00:08:10.280 --> 00:08:12.840
People will be coming from outside 
the school for the festival,

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.390
so do your best.

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:18.390
Azuma-sensei, bring your 
girlfriend to the festival!

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.340
What?

00:08:19.900 --> 00:08:25.480
Unfortunately, I don't have 
a girlfriend at the moment.

00:08:25.740 --> 00:08:27.310
What a surprise.

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:29.680
I figured you'd be popular.

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:32.210
You're so kind and handsome, after all.

00:08:32.210 --> 00:08:35.250
Maybe he doesn't want to settle on just one!

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.660
He's got a new girl every day.

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:38.740
That's not it.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:44.300
I just don't like bubbly girls.

00:08:44.300 --> 00:08:47.000
I've never been any good with them.

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.470
Really?

00:08:49.470 --> 00:08:51.760
<i>He's always been popular...</i>

00:08:52.070 --> 00:08:54.330
Where's Tsukahara-kun?

00:08:54.330 --> 00:08:56.010
Kanamecchi is...

00:08:56.010 --> 00:08:58.290
What about me?

00:08:58.290 --> 00:08:59.010
Huh?

00:08:59.480 --> 00:09:01.530
Yuki, monkey...

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:04.060
What are you doing?

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:05.630
Kanamecchi!

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:08.820
Huh? W-Wait— Yukki!

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:13.870
Don't you realize there's no time for this?

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:15.890
Ow!

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:19.050
Why me?

00:09:19.050 --> 00:09:24.120
The extended homeroom period has ended 
and you guys were doing nothing.

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.070
Shun and Yuta, head 
back to your classroom.

00:09:26.070 --> 00:09:27.570
Your class rep is worried.

00:09:27.570 --> 00:09:30.870
Oh, right. We were in the 
middle of making flowers.

00:09:30.870 --> 00:09:32.350
You two, as well.

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:33.590
Okay.

00:09:39.350 --> 00:09:41.090
Looks like you have lots on your plate.

00:09:42.110 --> 00:09:44.990
It's nothing new.

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:47.560
Don't push yourself too hard.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.320
I'm not...

00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:07.500
Matsuoka-kun, Asaba-kun.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.040
Which costume do you want to wear at the festival?

00:10:12.800 --> 00:10:15.630
These are so cute. I don't 
know which to choose.

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:16.690
You can't choose?

00:10:16.690 --> 00:10:17.420
What?

00:10:17.420 --> 00:10:20.700
I'm sure you two would look good in anything!

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:21.390
I know.

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:22.680
Really?

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:33.670
Cheshire!

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:37.370
I bet they'd look good in these, too!

00:10:37.370 --> 00:10:38.450
What?

00:10:39.830 --> 00:10:40.860
Yukki.

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:44.810
This will be our first time...

00:10:45.300 --> 00:10:46.750
Our first time...

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:48.370
Chizuru-san...

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:51.620
You're not in middle school any more.

00:10:51.620 --> 00:10:55.210
Stop getting excited every time 
someone says it's their first time.

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.590
You're just using the 
copier for the first time.

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:00.440
Sorry, sorry.

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:02.710
Yukki, have you used a copier before?

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:04.300
It's my first time, too.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:06.500
Yukki, it's your first time, too!

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:08.180
Starting copying.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:09.140
Your first... first time...

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:16.820
Huh? It's blank?!

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:23.030
I think it's trying to throw us 
off by refusing to copy anything.

00:11:23.030 --> 00:11:25.600
Sorry, can I skip ahead of you?

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:26.680
I'm in a hurry.

00:11:26.680 --> 00:11:28.230
Go ahead.

00:11:38.530 --> 00:11:40.670
Ah, so that's how you do it...

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:43.010
Place the original face down!

00:11:43.250 --> 00:11:45.510
Allow me to copy that technique!

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:49.670
Don't you feel we're getting 
better at making copies...

00:11:49.670 --> 00:11:51.520
because we're copying others?

00:11:51.960 --> 00:11:53.540
Spot on.

00:11:54.640 --> 00:11:58.530
As experts at copying, 
we'll get it right this time...

00:11:58.840 --> 00:11:59.810
What?

00:11:59.810 --> 00:12:01.280
What is this?

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:05.610
They keep coming!

00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:07.170
Sorry.

00:12:07.170 --> 00:12:10.390
Kaname asked for eight 
sheets, so I pushed eight.

00:12:10.390 --> 00:12:11.290
What?

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:13.750
How do we stop this thing?

00:12:13.980 --> 00:12:15.890
Hey, stop! Stop!

00:12:15.890 --> 00:12:17.320
Good...

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:19.430
It's not good. Look.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:22.850
We made eight wasteful, failed copies.

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:25.090
How terrible for the planet.

00:12:25.380 --> 00:12:26.890
What's wrong with this thing?

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:29.350
I thought technology was 
making our lives easier!

00:12:29.850 --> 00:12:36.590
The advances of technology must 
be so great that humans can't keep up.

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:42.360
It won't be long before 
robots turn against humans.

00:12:42.360 --> 00:12:43.800
That is indeed possible.

00:12:44.190 --> 00:12:45.860
What are you, stupid?

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:47.370
Kaname.

00:12:47.740 --> 00:12:50.750
I only asked for eight copies.

00:12:50.750 --> 00:12:52.980
How much time are you wasting over it?

00:13:00.720 --> 00:13:03.840
Wow, Kanamecchi! You're brilliant!

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:06.870
And you're brilliant... at being stupid.

00:13:07.920 --> 00:13:09.600
There you are.

00:13:09.600 --> 00:13:15.180
We're asking people what they 
want to do during the festival.

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:18.110
We'll be right there.

00:13:19.610 --> 00:13:21.690
Tsukahara-senpai! Good timing!

00:13:22.120 --> 00:13:27.240
Three classes want to use the home 
economics classroom during the festival.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:30.680
Their reps are arguing over it in the 
Student Council Office right now.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:31.660
What?

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:33.970
Senpai, do something!

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:35.960
Do something?

00:13:35.960 --> 00:13:37.540
Kaname, aren't you coming?

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:39.200
Huh? Um...

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:40.800
Senpai, hurry.

00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:43.190
Okay, I'm coming.

00:13:43.190 --> 00:13:45.790
Yuki, could you... the names...

00:13:45.790 --> 00:13:48.430
I mean, the place where you...

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:52.380
Huh? What?

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:52.380
Reception! The reception desk!

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:55.430
Put my name down for that!

00:13:56.650 --> 00:14:00.350
Reception? Boring.

00:14:00.350 --> 00:14:02.110
He's stumbling over his words...

00:14:13.940 --> 00:14:15.470
Hey, Princess.

00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:17.810
What are you doing?

00:14:20.090 --> 00:14:23.530
We're getting fitted for our 
outfits for the festival.

00:14:23.530 --> 00:14:25.710
We're waiting to be tacked.

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:29.490
Yuki! Monkey! Where are you?

00:14:28.790 --> 00:14:30.610
Uh-oh, it's Kanamecchi!

00:14:30.610 --> 00:14:32.100
Didn't take him long to notice.

00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:35.580
Did you do something to make him mad again?

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.370
Um...

00:14:40.240 --> 00:14:42.060
Can you hide us for a bit?

00:14:42.060 --> 00:14:43.110
What?

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:45.530
Damn it, where'd they go?

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:50.610
Shun, Yuta, have you seen 
Yuki and the monkey?

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:51.470
Nope.

00:14:51.470 --> 00:14:53.800
No, is something wrong?

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:58.430
I said I wanted to work at 
reception during the festival,

00:14:58.430 --> 00:15:00.370
but I'm signed up to be a ghost.

00:15:00.720 --> 00:15:03.020
I know they did it.

00:15:04.520 --> 00:15:06.990
You guys look rather fetching.

00:15:06.990 --> 00:15:09.630
What are those, your outfits for...

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:12.670
Sorry.

00:15:15.570 --> 00:15:16.620
Hey.

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:19.020
Let me look under your skirt.

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:20.020
What?

00:15:20.020 --> 00:15:21.910
Let me see what's under there.

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:23.020
D-Don't do...

00:15:23.020 --> 00:15:24.470
Just let me see.

00:15:24.470 --> 00:15:26.110
I can't do that.

00:15:26.110 --> 00:15:26.780
Why not?

00:15:27.210 --> 00:15:30.450
Kaname-san, what a bold pervert you are.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:32.700
What? That's not what this is!

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:37.250
You think I'd enjoy looking up his skirt?

00:15:37.250 --> 00:15:38.740
What do you mean?

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:42.670
There might be a world 
unknown to you under there.

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:44.460
What are you talking about?

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.260
Are you stupid?

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:46.260
Yutan, nice!

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:48.710
Keep distracting him!

00:15:49.030 --> 00:15:52.850
Don't argue!

00:15:52.850 --> 00:15:55.340
I'm wearing a jersey under here!

00:15:55.340 --> 00:15:56.410
Then...

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:59.730
You shouldn't have any problems 
with letting me take a look!

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:02.140
Let me look.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.020
No!

00:16:06.120 --> 00:16:07.790
Enough already...

00:16:13.890 --> 00:16:14.870
You pervert.

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:17.120
This isn't what it looks like!

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:22.500
Awful! You're awful!

00:16:22.500 --> 00:16:24.630
How dare you! How dare 
you do that to Shun-chan!

00:16:23.450 --> 00:16:24.630
You've got the wrong...

00:16:25.570 --> 00:16:28.550
Hey! Don't think you'll get away!

00:16:29.380 --> 00:16:33.060
You've been awfully cranky lately.

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:38.270
Being cranky's practically his hobby.

00:16:38.270 --> 00:16:39.890
Whose fault do you think that is?

00:16:41.680 --> 00:16:44.140
Kaname, can you make enlarged copies?

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:46.210
Huh? Why?

00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:52.650
The Manga Society asked me to make 
enlarged copies for their posters.

00:16:52.650 --> 00:16:54.060
You do it.

00:16:54.060 --> 00:16:57.370
I can't believe you're asking me 
for favors after I got mad at you.

00:16:58.860 --> 00:17:00.520
Fine.

00:17:00.520 --> 00:17:02.670
I suppose I'll have to help, considering how bad–

00:17:02.670 --> 00:17:03.580
Tsukahara!

00:17:04.240 --> 00:17:05.720
Come with me.

00:17:05.720 --> 00:17:07.790
Something terrible's happened.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:09.320
Sure.

00:17:09.960 --> 00:17:12.330
Can your copies wait? I have to...

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:14.380
Huh? Sure.

00:17:14.380 --> 00:17:16.970
Tsukahara, this way. Hurry!

00:17:17.460 --> 00:17:18.390
Okay.

00:18:37.380 --> 00:18:39.890
<b>Blackout curtain</b>

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:44.200
What is this? Blackout curtains?

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:45.890
Blackout–

00:18:47.820 --> 00:18:49.140
Blackout curtains?

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:51.650
There's none left.

00:18:54.560 --> 00:18:56.200
N-None?

00:18:56.200 --> 00:18:57.070
Yes.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:18:58.300
Not a single one?

00:18:58.300 --> 00:18:59.410
Y-Yes.

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.410
S-Senpai?

00:19:10.900 --> 00:19:13.690
Your class is putting on a haunted house?

00:19:13.690 --> 00:19:15.930
That will need tons of curtains.

00:19:15.930 --> 00:19:18.170
You should've turned in 
your request sooner...

00:19:19.120 --> 00:19:20.320
Senpai?

00:19:21.820 --> 00:19:23.080
You're right.

00:19:23.080 --> 00:19:25.610
We're running a haunted house. Right.

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:27.220
I'm right?

00:19:27.730 --> 00:19:31.790
You'll have to change it into something 
simple to prepare, or...

00:19:31.790 --> 00:19:33.980
That won't be easy.

00:19:33.980 --> 00:19:36.060
Yeah, but...

00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:38.490
It's okay.

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:45.870
A bunch of classes took too many 
just in case they needed them.

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:49.710
You should have enough 
if you borrow some from them.

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:51.120
I see.

00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.590
You're right.

00:19:59.870 --> 00:20:02.770
Your request has been approved.

00:20:02.770 --> 00:20:03.640
Here.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:05.920
Good luck with your haunted house.

00:20:07.240 --> 00:20:08.200
Thanks.

00:20:09.700 --> 00:20:12.650
We're almost done with props...

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:15.610
All the roles have been decided...

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:17.160
Where are the curtains?

00:20:18.500 --> 00:20:21.070
Tsukahara, what happened to the curtains?

00:20:21.070 --> 00:20:23.680
Huh? I got some.

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:25.660
Thanks a lot.

00:20:25.970 --> 00:20:30.390
You shouldn't make others 
do your work for you!

00:20:30.390 --> 00:20:33.920
So what? Tsukahara's more reliable than me.

00:20:33.920 --> 00:20:36.050
You're useless!

00:20:36.050 --> 00:20:37.420
You're so mean.

00:20:39.780 --> 00:20:43.250
Shun-chan, I'm gonna be a ghost.

00:20:43.250 --> 00:20:44.700
What kind do you think I should be?

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:47.250
Let's see...

00:20:47.710 --> 00:20:49.980
How do you feel about spandex?

00:20:49.980 --> 00:20:52.430
Spandex? Why would I wear that?

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:55.940
Yuki, is the Manga Society doing 
anything for the festival?

00:20:57.090 --> 00:20:58.470
A manga cafe.

00:20:58.470 --> 00:21:00.430
Apparently, they do it every year.

00:21:00.430 --> 00:21:01.440
I see.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:06.550
Yuki, I haven't copied the 
posters for the Manga Society yet.

00:21:06.550 --> 00:21:07.700
Can it wait until tomorrow?

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:09.400
Huh? Forget about it.

00:21:09.400 --> 00:21:10.540
I already did it.

00:21:11.710 --> 00:21:14.390
Well, Yuta did it for me.

00:21:15.490 --> 00:21:18.820
Yuta said he knew how to 
make enlarged copies, too.

00:21:18.820 --> 00:21:22.000
I might as well have him 
do it if I'm asking you.

00:21:22.790 --> 00:21:24.300
What does that mean?

00:21:24.300 --> 00:21:29.140
You're working so hard, I 
wasn't sure you could fit it in.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:31.880
I reckoned it'd only turn out well by sheer luck.

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:34.270
Yeah, you're so unreliable.

00:21:34.270 --> 00:21:35.770
I know what you mean.

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:43.780
Kanamecchi? Is something wrong?

00:21:44.570 --> 00:21:46.230
I get it!

00:21:47.500 --> 00:21:52.310
Ow! Why only me?

00:21:53.600 --> 00:21:57.960
Don't fight before the festival.

00:21:56.430 --> 00:21:59.840
The days leading up to the 
festival were like a storm.

00:22:00.140 --> 00:22:03.530
If I lost focus for a 
minute, I'd be swept away.

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:03.530
Kaname-kun, don't be angry...

00:22:04.950 --> 00:22:10.350
But if I get swept away, I'd 
see a change of scenery.

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:12.310
I'm mad! I'm really steaming now!

00:22:12.310 --> 00:22:14.990
You won't believe the ghost I'll make you be!

00:22:14.990 --> 00:22:16.540
Bring it on.

00:22:16.540 --> 00:22:19.360
I'll use my Student Council 
influence to make you perform...

00:22:19.360 --> 00:22:22.030
a Hyottoko dance by 
yourself at the festival.

00:22:22.030 --> 00:22:24.570
What? No!

00:22:25.460 --> 00:22:28.390
Kaname, that's an obvious abuse of power...

00:22:28.390 --> 00:22:31.370
Of course it is. Power's no 
good if you don't use it.

00:22:31.370 --> 00:22:33.970
Shun-chan, Kanamecchi's being mean!

00:22:33.970 --> 00:22:36.540
Careful, Chizuru-kun!

00:24:16.690 --> 00:24:19.030
Next time: On your mark.
